{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/321451-playable-changling-concept","id":321451,"title":"Playable Changling Concept","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-24T22:52:21-08:00","id":321451,"title":"Playable Changling Concept","content":"I am working on a character concept for an up and coming Live Action Game. I have two different concepts in mind. I decided to take a step back and look at things from a LARP perspective. What kind of concept makes people come to you. Instead of having to worry about always going to someone else and initiating conversation, breaking the ice, etc. Then I thought of things that would be useful in a game. Healer, someone with Occular Ability. I mean most Venue Sheets have a section for PCs that have Occular abilities, or an Oracle is a great addition to any game. But the more I started thinking about it, a Concept came to me. A Healer, that uses Goblin Fruit, but is also a cook? When I put him to paper I made him a Spring Court (For Healing), Wizend Chirurgeon, Knight of the Knowledge of the Tongue. So basically he kind find Goblin Fruit in the hedge, use it to cook meals, and then heal other Changlings. i.e. After Encounters, I'll have the brutes, those damaged coming to me for healing purposes. Now the Chirurgeon is more medical then cook, so I thought about taking Holistic Awareness also, to show and taking a Specialty in Medicine of Medicinal Herbs, or Medicinal Food. Cooking soup for example, to further healing abilities. Of course then I noticed the Dual Kith Merit, and thought, that a Chirurgeon/Brewer might make a good mix. Since the Brewer adds in the idea of cooking something for example, then I could make wines/elixers/Tonics, etc that heal people, using Goblin Fruit. So I have these ideas, anyone have any suggestions on how to make them work good together? Right now we are not sure what Court the game is going to be set in, I like Spring, because of the EternalSpring Contract and Healing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4377-derekleighstark","name":"derekleighstark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4377_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}